# OpenCode harness: delegation by default

This rule is internal to this project/environment. It applies to every session that runs under the OpenCode harness.

## Default behavior

- For any multi-part task, split the work into independent packages before editing.
- Delegate each independent package to a separate subagent. Give every subagent the repository rules from `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, and require a report in English with file:line evidence.
- Use an isolated git worktree and branch per delegated package. Never let a subagent edit the main worktree.
- Review the complete diff of every subagent commit before integrating it. Integrate with `--no-ff` or an explicit cherry-pick, then run the full suite.
- Prefer thorough parallel verification over token savings. Token budget is not a reason to skip delegation, an independent audit, or a repeated measurement.

## When to run more subagents

- Add a dedicated subagent for each independent audit, benchmark investigation, or documentation consistency check.
- Keep benchmarks sequential even when subagents are parallel; concurrent builds and benchmark spawns corrupt timing measurements.

## Non-negotiable limits

- A subagent's claim is not evidence until the parent has seen the command output or reviewed the diff.
- Never claim a test, acceptance criterion, or performance improvement passed without running it.
- Never push, publish, tag, or change repository configuration from a delegated worktree.
- Do not touch untracked `assets/` or read home-directory credential files.
